@startuml
title UC17 - Select Starter Pokemon - Use Case Description

map "UC17 - Select Starter Pokemon" as UC17 {
  Name => Select Starter Pokemon
  ID => UC17
  Description => New player selects their first Pokemon from three starter options
  Actor => Player
  Organizational Benefits => Critical onboarding experience establishing player identity and team foundation
  Trigger => Player logs in for the first time after registration (UC18)
  Preconditions => 1. Player has successfully registered (UC18) and logged in (UC1) \n 2. Player has no Pokemon in their team (first-time player)
  Postconditions => 1. Starter Pokemon added to player team \n 2. Story begins (UC6)
  Main Course => 1. System detects first-time player (empty team) \n 2. System displays starter selection screen \n 3. System presents three starter Pokemon (Fire, Water, Grass) \n 4. System shows each starter stats, type and description \n 5. Player selects one starter Pokemon \n 6. System confirms selection with player \n 7. System creates starter Pokemon via WorldGenService \n 8. System adds starter to player team \n 9. System saves player data and transitions to UC6
  Alternate Courses => 1. Player reviews different starters -> cycle through options \n 2. Player changes mind -> return to selection \n 3. Returning player (has Pokemon) -> skip starter selection
  Exceptions => 1. Starter data missing from pokemon.json -> display error \n 2. Save failure after selection -> retry save
}

@enduml
